    <bpmn:process id="W_W4821" name="W4821. CIAP/PCAB Board Engagement, Petitions &amp; Regulatory Liaison" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Regulatory change; rule-making petition; interpretation query; industry-association agenda (VS-104); dispute/appeal
Frequency: Ad hoc + via industry association
Volume: ~several engagements per year
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance / PCAB Compliance Lead
Participants: Government Affairs (VS-104), Trade Sales (VS-11), Legal (VS-100.3), industry associations
Source: workflow W4821 — CIAP/PCAB Board Engagement, Petitions &amp; Regulatory Liaison</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4821_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4821_Lane1" name="PCAB Compliance Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4821_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4821_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4821_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4821_Lane2" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4821_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4821_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4821_Start4" name="Regulatory change; rule-making petition; interpretation query; industry-association…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4821_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4821_Task5" name="Monitor CIAP/PCAB rule-making, circulars, and IRR changes (category thresholds…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monitor CIAP/PCAB rule-making, circulars, and IRR changes (category thresholds, project-registration rules, specialty-license scope, sustainability/green-build requirements); assess impact on BuildRight&#x27;s licenses and operations and feed changes to the strategy (W4817) and portfolio (VS-166)
Responsible (R): PCAB Compliance Lead / Government Affairs
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4821_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4821_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4821_Task6" name="Engage the board on interpretations, petitions, or industry positions (alone or…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Engage the board on interpretations, petitions, or industry positions (alone or via construction-industry associations — links to VS-104); file petitions/comments on proposed rules affecting the retail-contractor model, B2G material-and-install scope, or category economics
Responsible (R): PCAB Compliance Lead / Legal / Government Affairs
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Ad hoc</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4821_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4821_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4821_Task7" name="Manage disputes/appeals (license-condition dispute, denial, penalty — W4838)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Manage disputes/appeals (license-condition dispute, denial, penalty — W4838) through PCAB/CIAP and, if needed, the Office of the President/courts (VS-100); document positions and outcomes in the legal matter record (VS-100.3) and analytics (W4839)
Responsible (R): Legal / PCAB Compliance Lead
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per dispute</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4821_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4821_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4821_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4821_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-725 (ensure controlled execution — PCAB Licensing Strategy, Entity Registration &amp; Lifecycle (PA-165.1).) | - CTL-725: regulatory changes assessed and logged; petitions/disputes approved by VP Legal; positions documented
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance / PCAB Compliance Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
